---
import CaseStudyLayout from "@/layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro";
import SectionHeading from "@/components/SectionHeading.astro";
import Figure from "@/components/Figure.astro";

const tocItems = [
  { id: "the-problem", label: "The problem we walked into" },
  { id: "research", label: "Research that shaped everything" },
  { id: "designing", label: "Designing for clarity and speed" },
  { id: "from-design-to-impact", label: "From design to impact" },
  { id: "reflection", label: "What this work reinforced" },
];
---

<CaseStudyLayout
  title="Gotandem: Redesigning B2B Procurement for Maximum Impact"
  description="A product design case study: redesigning a B2B procurement platform to boost purchase completion, cut approval times, and deliver measurable business impact."
  date="2019-01-21"
  dateFormatted="January 21, 2019"
  tocItems={tocItems}
>
  <p>
    I'm excited to share the work I did on Gotandem. Gotandem is a B2B procurement platform
    that helps companies centralize purchasing and control spend. Teams across offices,
    coworking spaces, and retail chains can source, approve, and track recurring
    purchases, everything from office supplies to pantry goods, through a single system.
  </p>

  <p>
    I led product design and go-to-market initiatives, focusing on conversion, operational
    efficiency, and user satisfaction.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>Role:</strong> Lead Product Designer (product design, go-to-market strategy,
    conversion optimization, and cross-functional collaboration with product and engineering).
  </p>

  <p>The backend was already powerful. The product experience didn't match it yet.</p>

  <Figure
    src="/assets/images/Gotandem01.avif"
    alt="Gotandem platform overview, the redesigned procurement dashboard"
    caption="The redesigned Gotandem platform, centralizing procurement into one clear experience."
    width={1920}
    height={1080}
    loading="eager"
  />

  <SectionHeading id="the-problem" title="The problem we walked into" />

  <p>
    The interface felt outdated, inconsistent, and cluttered. Core workflows like sourcing,
    approvals, and recurring orders were full of friction. Navigation was unclear. UI patterns
    weren't standardized. Users often felt overwhelmed rather than in control.
  </p>

  <p>
    The real challenge was simplifying complexity: bringing consistency, clarity, and
    confidence to a high-frequency B2B procurement workflow without stripping away the power
    that made the platform valuable in the first place.
  </p>

  <p>
    I partnered closely with product and engineering. We ran tight feedback loops, staying
    aligned from early exploration through final handoff so that what we shipped was both
    usable and strategically sound.
  </p>

  <Figure
    src="/assets/images/Gotandem02.webp"
    alt="Before and after comparison of the Gotandem interface"
    caption="Bringing consistency and clarity to a cluttered procurement interface."
    width={1920}
    height={1080}
  />

  <SectionHeading id="research" title="Research that shaped everything" />

  <p>
    We talked to procurement managers, finance teams, and the people actually placing orders.
    We mapped their current workflows and found the same friction points again and again:
    long approval chains, confusing product catalogs, and almost no visibility into recurring
    orders.
  </p>

  <p>
    Quantitative data confirmed what the interviews suggested. Checkout and approval flows
    had clear drop-off points. People were abandoning processes that should have felt routine.
    Those insights became the foundation for the redesign.
  </p>

  <Figure
    src="/assets/images/Gotandem03.avif"
    alt="Research findings mapped to user workflow pain points"
    caption="Mapping friction points across the procurement workflow, from checkout to approvals."
    width={1920}
    height={1080}
  />

  <SectionHeading id="designing" title="Designing for clarity and speed" />

  <p>
    We simplified the ordering flow into a single-screen multi-item checkout. Managers
    received role-based dashboards that provided real-time visibility into team spend and
    recurring orders. We introduced smart recommendations and recurring order templates to
    cut decision fatigue and accelerate approvals.
  </p>

  <Figure
    src="/assets/images/Gotandem04.avif"
    alt="The simplified single-screen multi-item checkout flow"
    caption="Single-screen multi-item checkout, reducing steps and decision fatigue."
    width={1920}
    height={1080}
  />

  <p>
    Micro-interactions, notifications, and progress indicators were prototyped and tested
    with engineering. Small signals of progress and clarity built trust in a process that
    used to feel opaque.
  </p>

  <p>
    The loop looked like this: map the pain, design the simplified flow, prototype the
    critical moments, test with real users, measure the drop-off, refine, and ship. Then we
    did it again.
  </p>

  <Figure
    src="/assets/images/Gotandem05.avif"
    alt="Role-based dashboard showing team spend and recurring orders"
    caption="Role-based dashboards: real-time visibility into team spend and recurring orders."
    width={1920}
    height={1080}
  />

  <Figure
    src="/assets/images/Gotandem06.webp"
    alt="Smart recommendations and recurring order templates"
    caption="Smart recommendations and recurring order templates that accelerate approvals."
    width={1920}
    height={1080}
  />

  <SectionHeading id="from-design-to-impact" title="From design to impact" />

  <p>
    We partnered with sales and customer success to put the new onboarding and approval
    flows in front of pilot clients. Feedback and conversion analytics drove the next round
    of refinements. Nothing stayed theoretical for long.
  </p>

  <p>The results were concrete:</p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>+35%</strong> increase in purchase completion across multi-location accounts</li>
    <li>Approval time cut by <strong>50%</strong>, freeing managers for higher-value work</li>
    <li>NPS up <strong>22 points</strong>, driven by clearer dashboards and simpler workflows</li>
    <li>Higher client retention and increased average order volume from streamlined recurring orders</li>
  </ul>

  <Figure
    src="/assets/images/Gotandem07.webp"
    alt="Gotandem's redesigned approval and onboarding flow"
    caption="The redesigned approval flow: faster decisions, clearer status, happier teams."
    width={1920}
    height={1080}
  />

  <SectionHeading id="reflection" title="What this work reinforced" />

  <p>
    In B2B product design, understanding both user needs and business goals is
    non-negotiable. Small workflow improvements and clear visibility can move conversion and
    operational efficiency more than big feature launches. And close collaboration across
    design, engineering, and go-to-market teams is what turns good ideas into solutions that
    are actually actionable, scalable, and impactful.
  </p>

  <p>
    Gotandem already had the engine. We redesigned the experience so that engine could finally
    deliver the control and confidence its users needed. The numbers showed it worked. More
    importantly, the people using it every day felt the difference.
  </p>

  <blockquote>
    <p>
      Gotandem already had the engine. We redesigned the experience so that engine could
      finally deliver the control and confidence its users needed.
    </p>
    <cite>Masudur Rahman</cite>
  </blockquote>

  <Fragment slot="footer">
    <h3 class="text-base font-semibold mt-0 mb-2">Key outcomes</h3>
    <ul class="mb-5">
      <li>+35% purchase completion, 50% faster approvals, NPS up 22 points</li>
      <li>Simplified multi-item checkout and role-based dashboards for real-time spend visibility</li>
      <li>Smart recommendations and recurring order templates that cut decision fatigue</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mb-5">
      If you're working on B2B procurement tools, or thinking about conversion-first
      product design, I'd love to hear from you.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</CaseStudyLayout>
